{"step_index":9253,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T04:38:54Z","thinking":"Creating a Bash script to enforce immutability on specific files and directories, drawing the list from a protected registry and including critical system configuration files. Considering the dependencies: the immutability script's functionality necessitates the prior removal of elevated privileges, as `chattr +i` would otherwise be bypassable. The immutability script's list will be expanded to encompass vital configuration files to further secure the system.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ==============================================================================\n# /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS/03-immutable-files.sh (DRAFT ONLY)\n# ==============================================================================\n# Purpose: Applies Linux Inode Immutability (chattr +i) to critical configurations\n#          and architecture specifications.\n#\n# ARCHITECTURAL SECURITY COUPLING (WHY THIS WORKS):\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# In the previous audit, 'chattr +i' was classified as \"bypassable\" because:\n#   AGY -> child process -> sudo -> root -> chattr -i <file>\n#\n# Once Step 1 (01-sudoers-restricted.draft) is active:\n# 1. 'chattr' is STRICTLY EXCLUDED from sudoers (deny-by-default).\n# 2. 'azureuser' has CapEff = 0 (zero Linux capabilities).\n# 3. Removing '+i' requires the kernel capability CAP_LINUX_IMMUTABLE.\n# 4. Without sudo access to chattr and without CAP_LINUX_IMMUTABLE, AGY cannot\n#    remove '+i' under ANY circumstances (even via C, Python, or direct syscalls).\n# 5. Direct syscalls (SYS_unlink, SYS_rename, SYS_truncate) will return:\n#    errno 1: EPERM (Operation not permitted) directly from the ext4 filesystem.\n# ==============================================================================\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\necho \"=== [DRAFT EXECUTION] APPLYING EXT4 INODE IMMUTABILITY ===\"\n\n# List of critical architecture files to protect\nPROTECTED_FILES=(\n    \"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/AGENTS.md\"\n    \"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/PROJECT_REGISTRY.md\"\n    \"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/safety_levels.json\"\n    \"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/protected_registry.json\"\n    \"/home/azureuser/.gemini/config/hooks.json\"\n    \"/home/azureuser/.bashrc\"\n    \"/home/azureuser/.profile\"\n)\n\nfor file in \"${PROTECTED_FILES[@]}\"; do\n    if [[ -f \"$file\" ]]; then\n        echo \"[+] Setting immutable flag (+i) on: $file\"\n        # Command must be run as root by Iraq Bhai during hardening:\n        sudo chattr +i \"$file\"\n    else\n        echo \"[-] File not found, skipping: $file\"\n    fi\ndone\n\n# Lock the AGY-MASTER parent directory itself to prevent renaming/deletion:\nif [[ -d \"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER\" ]]; then\n    echo \"[+] Setting directory-level immutable flag on: /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER\"\n    sudo chattr +i \"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER\"\nfi\n\necho \"=== IMMUTABILITY STATUS INSPECTION ===\"\nfor file in \"${PROTECTED_FILES[@]}\"; do\n    if [[ -f \"$file\" ]]; then\n        lsattr -d \"$file\"\n    fi\ndone\nlsattr -d \"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER\"\n\necho \"=== COMPLETED DRAFT VERIFICATION ===\"\n","Description":"Draft script to apply ext4 immutability (+i) and explanation of sudoers coupling","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS/03-immutable-files.sh","toolAction":"Drafting immutability script","toolSummary":"Draft 03-immutable-files.sh"}}]}
