{"step_index":9255,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T04:38:59Z","thinking":"Step four involves setting up an external, immutable backup using a WORM (Write Once Read Many) policy in Azure Blob Storage. This requires the use of command-line tools for configuration. A crucial constraint is that the configuration *must* be executed from outside the virtual machine to ensure proper immutability.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# EXTERNAL IMMUTABLE BACKUP ARCHITECTURE (WORM & REMOTE GIT)\n\nTarget Host: Azure VM `FatehAli`\nStatus: DRAFT SPECIFICATION (NO ACTIONS EXECUTED)\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHY EXTERNAL IMMUTABLE BACKUP IS MANDATORY\n\nEven with strict sudoers and `chattr +i`, an attacker or kernel failure could corrupt local disks.\nThe ONLY truly impenetrable defense against total VM compromise is **Storage Outside the VM**:\n- The VM possesses **ZERO Azure credentials** and **NO Managed Identity**.\n- Therefore, data stored in an Azure Blob Storage container with **Immutable Blob Storage (WORM - Write Once, Read Many)** cannot be deleted or overwritten by ANY process inside the VM.\n\n---\n\n## 2. AZURE BLOB WORM POLICY SETUP (EXECUTE FROM AZURE CLOUD SHELL)\n\n> 🛑 **CRITICAL OPERATIONAL REQUIREMENT:**\n> These Azure CLI commands **CANNOT** and **MUST NOT** be executed from inside the `FatehAli` VM.\n> They must be executed by Iraq Bhai from **Azure Cloud Shell** (https://shell.azure.com) or an external admin workstation.\n\n### Step 1: Create a Dedicated Backup Storage Account\n```bash\n# Set your target Azure variables\nRESOURCE_GROUP=\"fatehali-rg\"\nLOCATION=\"eastus\" # Or your VM region\nSTORAGE_ACCOUNT=\"fatehalibackupstorage$RANDOM\"\nCONTAINER_NAME=\"immutable-vm-backups\"\n\n# Create standard general-purpose v2 storage account\naz storage account create \\\n    --name \"$STORAGE_ACCOUNT\" \\\n    --resource-group \"$RESOURCE_GROUP\" \\\n    --location \"$LOCATION\" \\\n    --sku Standard_LRS \\\n    --kind StorageV2 \\\n    --allow-blob-public-access false\n\n# Create container\naz storage container create \\\n    --name \"$CONTAINER_NAME\" \\\n    --account-name \"$STORAGE_ACCOUNT\" \\\n    --auth-mode login\n```\n\n### Step 2: Configure Time-Based WORM Immutability Policy\n```bash\n# Create an immutability policy (e.g. 30 days retention where NO ONE can delete or overwrite)\n# Set policy mode to Unlocked first to test, then Locked for permanent WORM protection\naz storage container immutability-policy create \\\n    --account-name \"$STORAGE_ACCOUNT\" \\\n    --container-name \"$CONTAINER_NAME\" \\\n    --resource-group \"$RESOURCE_GROUP\" \\\n    --period 30 \\\n    --allow-protected-append-writes true\n\n# Once tested, lock the policy (CANNOT BE REVERTED EVEN BY AZURE ACCOUNT ROOT UNTIL PERIOD EXPIRES):\n# az storage container immutability-policy lock \\\n#     --account-name \"$STORAGE_ACCOUNT\" \\\n#     --container-name \"$CONTAINER_NAME\" \\\n#     --resource-group \"$RESOURCE_GROUP\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. AUTOMATED REMOTE GIT PUSH (DISASTER RECOVERY)\n\nFor code repositories like `Frappe-erp-Alco`, `alco_app`, and `AGY-MASTER`, pushing clean commits to an external private Git server (GitHub / GitLab) ensures that local deletion is instantly recoverable via `git clone`.\n\n### Draft Backup Cron Script: `/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS/git-sync-backup.sh`\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ==============================================================================\n# Daily Automated Git Backup Script (Draft)\n# ==============================================================================\nset -euo pipefail\n\nBACKUP_REPOS=(\n    \"/home/azureuser/Frappe-erp-Alco\"\n    \"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER\"\n)\n\nTIMESTAMP=$(date -u +\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\nfor repo in \"${BACKUP_REPOS[@]}\"; do\n    if [[ -d \"$repo/.git\" ]]; then\n        echo \"[+] Syncing repository: $repo at $TIMESTAMP\"\n        cd \"$repo\"\n        git add -A\n        # Commit only if there are changes\n        if ! git diff-index --quiet HEAD --; then\n            git commit -m \"Automated DR Snapshot: $TIMESTAMP\"\n            # Push to private remote using dedicated deploy key\n            # git push origin main\n        fi\n    fi\ndone\n```\n\n### Crontab Integration (Draft):\n```cron\n# Run every night at 02:00 AM UTC\n0 2 * * * /bin/bash /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS/git-sync-backup.sh >> /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/REPORTS/daily/git-backup.log 2>&1\n```\n","Description":"External immutable backup architecture guide with Azure CLI WORM commands and Git sync script","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS/04-external-backup-setup.md","toolAction":"Drafting external backup architecture","toolSummary":"Draft 04-external-backup-setup"}}]}
